    <profile name="Aegis of The Emperor" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="b102-9930-151f-c83e">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">Models with the Aegis of the Emperor special rule have a 5+ invulnerable save. In Addition, roll a D6 each time a model with this ability suffers a mortal wound On a 6 that mortal wound is ignored.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Airborne Hunters" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="b816-55c6-e624-76fe">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">During deployment, you can set up this unit high in the skies instead of setting it up on the battlefield. If you do, at the end of one of your Movement phases you can set up this unit anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 9&quot; away from any enemy models.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="From Golden Light" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="dfe0-4c89-df93-7dad">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">During deployment, you can set up this model in a Godstrike-pattern teleportarium array instead of placing it on the battlefield. At the end of any of your movement phases this model can teleport into battle - set it up anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 9&quot; away from any enemy models</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Impaling Lunge" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="c15b-720f-658d-e59c">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">After this model finishes a charge move, you can select one enemy unit within 1&quot; of it and roll one D6; on a 4+ that enemy unit suffers D3 mortal wounds.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Slayers of Tyrants" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="cba5-2b8b-2c48-7810">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">When models in this unit pile in and consolidate, they can move up to 3&quot; towards the nearest enemy CHARACTER even if it is not the nearest enemy model, so long as they finish this move within 1&quot; of an enemy unit.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Inspirational Fighter" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="2fb8-d514-0572-f3a9">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">You can re-roll hit rolls of 1 made for friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES units within 6&quot; of this model.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Martial Inspiration" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="ea03-41f1-8cc6-994e">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">Once per battle, in your Charge phase, this model’s unit is eligible to declare a charge in a turn which it Advanced.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Swift Onslaught" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="24f0-3cef-d27d-ffac">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">While this model is leading a unit, you can re-roll Charge rolls made for that unit</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Vaultswords" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapons" hidden="false" id="76f2-885a-08b0-a038">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="4c40-c12d-8d74-1fe7">Melee</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="b392-8288-2208-6ab2">Melee</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="b6e6-61d9-0a48-2696">+1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="15b5-fbf0-b823-d985">-2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="D" typeId="805f-6ece-e727-1ac1">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Abilities" typeId="90e1-1023-d27e-1bb2">Sustained Hits, Precision, Extra Attacks 2, Parry Weapon</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Master of the Stances" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="3550-0fb2-6286-62f4">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">Once Per battle you may select one friendly unit within 12&quot; you may change the Martial Ka&apos;tah that unit is using.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Flare Shield" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="c223-a1c6-30e4-9ccb">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">This model has a 5+ Invulnerable Save</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Gravitic Backwash" typeId="10e3-235b-fd89-87a6" typeName="Abillities" hidden="false" id="6625-b0e1-76c1-497b">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1eb-0258-504f-a2f2">If any units with this ability are chosen as targets of a charge, subtract 2 from the charge roll.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Martial Ka&apos;tah" id="0aa6-8bbc-d60c-cbb7" hidden="false">
      <description>During your Command Phase each Unit with this special rule may choose which Fighting style they would like to use for this phase, Once chosen the unit may not change it&apos;s Style until the following turn. Each Style is Listed Below (If you are just reading this rule or did not remmeber until just know use the Rendax stance as it is the Default)


1. Dacatarai, While this Style is active Custodian models with this Special rule Gain the Lance Charge and Against the Odds SR. However models cannot use the Parry Special Rule


2. Rendax, While this Style is active, Custodian Models Gains +1 Attack and Must use one attack to Parry an incoming attack. if a Character model is within look out sir range this unit the unit gains a 6+ Feel no Pain and +1 to Look out sir Tests.


3. Soliari, While this Style is Active, Custodian Models weapons must be Used to Parry incoming attacks to protect Themselves, only one attack per model may be used to Make a normal Attack. all Parry attacks made by this unit may re-roll hit roles of 1, if a character model is within look out sir range this unit gains a 4+ Feel no pain and Automatically pass look out sir test for that character</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Parry" id="548b-c6b2-8283-1969" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the Close Combat Phase A Model with this special rule may choose to parry instead of Attacking. When doing so After a enemy model has made attacks targeting a model in this unit this model rolls hit roles as normal for it&apos;s weapon for each successful hit you may remove one successful hit roll from your opponents attacks. you can only parry equal to the number of attacks your model has. If you weapon has the Extra attacks or sweeping Special rules may still Allocate these attacks to Parrying but must use all there attacks to do so</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Parry Weapon" id="b277-5b4b-5409-dbc3" hidden="false">
      <description>A Weapon with this special Rule may parry attacks and still deal damage with this weapon, Parry weapons role to wound as well and if successful Deal half damage instead of normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Against The Odds" id="db5b-2c16-5e58-b7aa" hidden="false">
      <description>While a Model with this special Rule is in close combat with 5 or more enemy models gain an extra attack for every 5 models in that unit.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
